cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "SDT AI Agents: Specifications for a Reproducible Social Digital Twin Pipeline"
message: "If you refer to this work, please cite it using the metadata below. Cite the archived release, not the repository's current state."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Qanazi"
    given-names: "Saleh"
    affiliation: "TVES Laboratory, Université de Lille"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8860-9667"
    email: "saleh.qanaze@najah.edu"
abstract: >-
  Full specifications for three researcher-defined AI agents used to construct
  a Social Digital Twin from social media traces, institutional documents, and
  urban spatial data. The repository publishes the prompt specifications, input
  and output schemas, processing rules, validation procedures, and
  reproducibility protocol for a data preparation agent, a social interpretation
  agent, and a validation agent. Reproducibility rests on a published
  specification, a fixed output schema, source traceability, and empirically
  measured output variance, rather than on deterministic model behaviour.
keywords:
  - social digital twin
  - urban digital twin
  - smart city
  - social sensing
  - large language models
  - AI agents
  - reproducibility
  - socio-technical systems
  - urban renewal
